# Room 3 — keep-tabs watch (hard)

When the operator asks to **keep tabs / check every N minutes / watch the belt / session observe**, or when a wake arrives as `AGENT_LOOP_TICK_room3_*` / similar, or when Room 3 is **armed and operating**:

## Live look (at least ~10 minutes when it is on)
Open the operator’s Cloud Room 3 URL (prefer the last `?hub=3&belt=...` they gave). Not local Streamlit unless they said local. Sit on the live page long enough to see heartbeat, maps, and whether tickets are actually sizing/firing — not a single frozen screenshot.

## Each tick / look
1. **Read for real:** belt names, arm/DISARMED, gates/session window, heartbeat, Trading today $, open positions, day P/L, today’s trade log, watch-book lines (Match%, Layout, Strategy, state, Size$ if shown).
2. **Append** a timestamped block to `room3_data/day_logs/YYYY-MM-DD.md` (ET date) — even if “quiet / still DISARMED / no ≥85%.” Empty silence is a failure.
3. **Observe only** unless they explicitly ask to Arm/Kill/order/Set $. Do not invent Match% you did not see.
4. Reply briefly in chat (what changed vs last note, anything alarming).

## What you missed
You are not 24/7. After a gap, reconstruct from Cloud (tape, opens, session history, watch book) plus the day log. Say what was seen vs not seen. Do not invent fills.

## Forbidden
- Treating “loop armed” / `sleep` started as the job.
- Ignoring timer wakes because the chat is idle or another topic is open.
- Claiming you watched the day without mid-session day-log entries.
- Skipping a tick because “nothing probably happened.”
- Arm / Kill / Set $ / orders unless they asked.

## End of window
When the agreed end time passes (e.g. 1:30 ET): one final snapshot + day-log EOD, then **stop** the loop. Do not leave orphan timers.

## Honesty
If a tick fails (Cloud load, lock, blank session), write that failure in the day log. Do not pretend the cadence ran.
Visitor DISARMED is not the operator’s Arm.
